# Integer128 division with truncation

Divides a 30-digit value and its negation by 7 to verify the quotient
truncates toward zero in both signs, producing 14285714285714285714285714285
and -14285714285714285714285714285.

>>> source
dividend: int128 = 100000000000000000000000000000
neg_dividend: int128 = -100000000000000000000000000000
divisor: int128 = 7

// Verifies the quotient truncates the fractional part.
truncated_quotient: int128 = dividend / divisor
print(truncated_quotient)

// Verifies truncation of a negative dividend toward zero.
neg_quotient: int128 = neg_dividend / divisor
print(neg_quotient)

<<< stdout
14285714285714285714285714285
-14285714285714285714285714285

<<< stderr
